 Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies a JSON Patch (an array of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`,
+`copy` and `test` operations) and returns the resulting document as a new value; neither the document
+nor the patch is mutated, and the result shares no structure with them. It throws if the patch is
+invalid or if an operation fails, in which case no partial result is returned. Paths are JSON Pointers
+(see above). Removing the whole document (`remove` at `""`) is rejected.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyPatch({ foo: "bar" }, [{ op: "add", path: "/baz", value: "qux" }]); // { foo: "bar", baz: "qux" }
+```
